  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING AND MANAGING NAMIBIA S KEY 1 AND KEY 2 BLACK RHINO POPULATIONS FOR MAXIMUM GROWTH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT BY FACILITATING OPERATIONS TO PROTECT CRITICALLY ENDANGERED BLACK RHINOCEROS IN NAMIBIA, THE STRONGHOLD FOR THE SOUTHWESTERN SUBSPECIES. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE CRITICALLY ENDANGERED BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT IN NAMIBIA BY ADDRESSING THE ONGOING POACHING CRISIS AND THE ECONOMIC IMPACT OF THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC. THIS PROJECT WILL PROVIDE SUPPORT TO THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FORESTRY AND TOURISM IN NAMIBIA, SAVE THE RHINO TRUST AND THE BLACK RHINO CUSTODIANSHIP PROGRAM FOR: (1) MANAGING THE BLACK RHINOCEROS METAPOPULATION TO ACHIEVE SUSTAINED AND POSITIVE POPULATION GROWTH (2) IMPROVING RHINOCEROS PROTECTION (3) EXPANDING COORDINATION AMONG STAKEHOLDERS INCLUDING PRIVATE LANDOWNERS (4) UNDERSTANDING THE IMPACTS OF BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT AND SECURITY FOR RHINOCEROS POPULATIONS, AND (5) IMPROVING LIVING CONDITIONS FOR STAFF AND PROVIDING NEEDED FIELD EQUIPMENT AND RESOURCES FOR THE PROTECTION OF BLACK RHINOCEROS.</narrative>
  </description>
